    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d74">

                <pb facs="0152" n="986" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg986"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 659.119/292</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-22T19:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 22, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7880. For Sheldon [from
                    War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 545. Embassy’s 10120, your 602, May 17, 6 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d74-f1"/>
                    We have announced today, effective immediately, the extension to Denmark of the
                    relaxation of the embargo on the list of non-essentials now exportable to
                    Holland and Sweden.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
